.\" GETH \- Geth Engine for Tracking Hardware
.\" Installed as geth.1 (the name follows the GETH_BINARY_NAME build option).
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt GETH 1
.Os Linux
.Sh NAME
.Nm geth
.Nd Geth Engine for Tracking Hardware \- a fast, lightweight terminal system monitor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Pp
With no option,
.Nm
starts the interactive dashboard.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a terminal dashboard that samples CPU, GPU (multiple cards), memory,
power, temperature, disk and network and draws them as real-time charts
inspired by the KDE System Monitor.
When the terminal speaks the Kitty graphics protocol or Sixel, each graph
is a pixel image with smooth anti-aliased lines and a soft translucent
fill; otherwise the charts are drawn in text (solid area charts for
single-series panels, one-dot braille lines for multi-series panels).
The active renderer can be cycled with the
.Sy g
key or forced with
.Sy -renderer .
It is built for transparent and blurred terminals: nothing is ever drawn
with a background color, so the terminal background shows through.
It never requires root, except optionally enabling RAPL CPU package power
through the shipped udev rule.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "  -render-frame COLSxROWS"
.It Sy -probe
List every data source, its availability and a fix hint, then exit.
This is the only mode in which a brief NVML enumeration session runs.
.It Sy -probe-terminal
Probe the terminal image capabilities (Kitty graphics protocol, Sixel,
cell pixel size), print them and the renderer the selection rules would
choose, and exit.
Needs a terminal; with none, it says so.
.It Sy -dump
Print human-readable samples to stdout and exit on interrupt.
.It Sy -json
Print samples as JSON, one object per sample.
.It Sy -demo
Use synthetic data; no hardware is accessed.
.It Sy "-interval Ar ms"
Sampling interval in milliseconds (default 1000, minimum 10).
Beats the value stored in the config file.
.It Sy "-count Ar n"
Stop after
.Ar n
samples (default: run until interrupted).
.It Sy "-render-frame Ar COLSxROWS"
Render a single frame at the given size to stdout and exit.
The sub-options
.Sy -warmup Ar n
(samples to collect first; default 60) and
.Sy -ansi
(emit full SGR escape codes instead of plain text) apply only here, as does
.Sy -script Ar events
(see below).
.It Sy "-render-png Ar COLSxROWS"
Composite a single frame \- the generated background, the text glyphs and,
in pixels mode, the graph rasters \- into an 8-bit RGB PNG written to
stdout, and exit.
Also accepts
.Sy -warmup Ar n ,
.Sy -demo ,
.Sy -renderer Ar mode ,
.Sy -theme Ar name
and
.Sy -script Ar events .
.It Sy "-layout-report Ar COLSxROWS"
Print the layout engine's decision (candidate scores, chosen layout,
per-panel rectangles) at the given size and exit.
.It Sy -perf
Benchmark relayout cost and layout-cache reuse, then exit.
.It Sy "-columns Ar n"
Pin the layout column count (UI, render and report).
.It Sy -stats
Print render/perf statistics on exit.
.It Sy "-color Ar mode"
Force a color mode:
.Sy truecolor ,
.Sy 256
or
.Sy 16 .
Default: auto-detect from
.Ev COLORTERM .
.It Sy "-renderer Ar mode"
Force the chart renderer for this run only (not saved):
.Sy pixels
or
.Sy text .
Default: the
.Sq Ar graph_renderer
value from the
.Sq general
section of the config file
(Sy auto
resolves to the optimized renderer — Kitty when the terminal
speaks it, else text; Sixel is experimental and is selected only with
.Sy pixels ).
.It Sy "-config Ar path"
Path to the config file (default:
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/geth/config.toml ,
then
.Pa ~/.config/geth/config.toml ).
.It Sy "-theme Ar name"
Theme to use: a built-in name or a custom theme file name.
Default: the
.Sq general
theme from the config.
.It Sy -list-themes
List the selectable themes (built-in and custom) and mark the active one.
Does not touch the hardware.
.It Sy -no-save
Never write the config file (read-only).
.It Sy "-script Ar events"
Valid with
.Sy -render-frame
and
.Sy -render-png
: replay a comma-separated list of synthetic events (keys,
.Sy enter ,
.Sy space ,
.Sy tab ,
.Sy up/down/left/right ,
.Sy click:X:Y )
before the single frame is rendered.
.It Sy -help , Sy -h
Show help and exit.
.It Sy -version
Print name and version, then exit.
.El
.Sh KEY BINDINGS
.Bl -tag -width "  Shift-Tab"
.It Sy "q / Esc / Ctrl-C"
Quit (pending settings are saved first).
.It Sy e
Open the panel manager.
.It Sy ?
Show help; any key closes it.
.It Sy space
Pause/resume the display (sampling continues).
.It Sy "Tab / Shift-Tab"
Focus the next/previous visible panel.
.It Sy x
Hide the focused panel.
.It Sy click
Focus the panel under the cursor.
.It Sy "+ / ="
Faster sampling interval (250 ms to 5 s).
.It Sy "- / _"
Slower sampling interval.
.It Sy t
Cycle the graph window (30 s to 10 m).
.It Sy c
Cycle the column count (auto, 1 to 8).
.It Sy T
Cycle the theme (saves the config).
.It Sy g
Cycle the graph renderer (pixels / text; saves the config).
.It Sy "Up / Down or j / k"
Scroll one row (when the page overflows).
.It Sy "PgUp / PgDn"
Scroll one page.
.It Sy "Home / End"
Scroll to the top / bottom.
.It Sy "mouse wheel"
Scroll (only while the page overflows).
.El
.Pp
In the panel manager:
.Sy Up / Down
or
.Sy j / k
select a row,
.Sy space
toggles visibility,
.Sy K / J
move the panel up/down,
.Sy r
renames it,
.Sy enter
opens the per-series submenu (
.Sy space
hides/shows a series),
.Sy d
resets the layout,
.Sy Esc
closes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/geth/config.toml
(or
.Pa ~/.config/geth/config.toml ):
the user configuration.
Installed packages never modify this file; removing it (or the whole
.Pa ~/.config/geth
directory) restores the defaults.
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/geth/themes/ :
custom theme files (TOML).
.It
.Pa /usr/share/geth/themes/example.toml :
the example theme shipped with the package.
.It
.Pa /usr/share/geth/99-geth-rapl.rules :
a udev rule that makes RAPL CPU package power readable without root.
It is shipped but not activated; copy it to
.Pa /etc/udev/rules.d/
to enable it.
.It
.Pa /usr/share/man/man1/geth.1 :
this manual page.
.It
.Pa /usr/share/doc/geth/README.md ,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/geth/CHANGELOG.md :
the project documentation.
.It
.Pa /usr/share/licenses/geth/LICENSE :
the MIT license.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XDG_CONFIG_HOME"
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the config file and the custom themes directory.
.It Ev HOME
Fallback base directory when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.It Ev COLORTERM
When set to
.Sy truecolor
or
.Sy 24bit ,
the truecolor mode is used; otherwise 256-color.
.It Ev GETH_TEST
Development guard: when set, saving the config file is refused anywhere
under the real
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the dashboard:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth
.Ed
.Pp
Demo data, no hardware:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --demo
.Ed
.Pp
Report which data sources are available:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --probe
.Ed
.Pp
Five JSON samples at 250 ms:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --json --count 5 --interval 250
.Ed
.Pp
Render one 120x40 frame with SGR colors (useful for screenshots):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --render-frame 120x40 --demo --ansi --warmup 30
.Ed
.Pp
Composite one 200x56 frame into a PNG file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --render-png 200x56 --demo > frame.png
.Ed
.Pp
Which image protocol does this terminal speak?
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --probe-terminal
.Ed
.Pp
Two columns with the amber theme:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
geth --columns 2 --theme amber
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
The binary is named
.Nm
by default.
If that clashes with Go-Ethereum's
.Nm geth
on your system, build with
.Sy -DGETH_BINARY_NAME=geth-engine .
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project README (
.Pa /usr/share/doc/geth/README.md
after installation, or
.Pa README.md
in the source tree) for configuration, themes, hardware support and
packaging documentation.
